it is a scene that people living along  this border have waited for for years a  line of Passenger cars crossed from  Colombia into Venezuela on Sunday  symbolically and practically ending  years of tense relations between the two  countries  it is really a great joy for all  Colombians to be able to move between  the two countries again many of us were  used to moving freely and it made us  very sad that for many years these two  countries were separated so we are very  happy  authorities reopened the tiendita's  bridge on January 1st with a festive by  national ceremony  balloons flew in the air while  government delegations met at the center  of a bridge that until recently had been  blocked by containers placed there by  the Venezuelan Army  today with this formal opening we  fulfilled a political will of President  Nicolas Maduro and Gustavo Petro of  total and transparent openness of the  border with Colombia  like this Colombian president Gustavo  Pedro had announced a normalization of  diplomatic relations with Venezuela  after winning elections in August the  two countries that gradually restored  border crossings and commerce since then  the shared 2200 kilometers border had  been partially closed seven years ago  and completely blocked in 2019 after the  Colombian president Ivan Duke questioned  Venezuelan president Nicolas maduro's  re-election  since then security along the border has  deteriorated with armed groups  controlling the legal transport of goods  and The Exodus of Venezuelan migrants  now people on both sides many by  national are hoping they will benefit  socially and economically  the former Brotherhood is back and this  is what the Venezuelan people want that  we build Brotherhood again that our  Venezuelan Brothers come through with  vehicles that they enter Colombia  because many people have their relatives  on the other side of the Border  trade between the two countries was  worth over 7 billion US Dollars back in  2008 but has collapsed to less than 300  million since while returning to those  levels will be difficult the reopening  has brought relief and hopes for better  times ahead Alessandra Al Jazeera Bogota
 

